WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.478
Right now, someone is playing GTA 6.

00:00:03.478 --> 00:00:04.968
It isn't you.

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:08.924
And the reason is a clock, not a server.

00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:11.554
GTA 6 doesn't launch once.

00:00:11.554 --> 00:00:16.240
It launches region by region — nineteen hours, start to finish.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.462
New Zealand hit midnight first. 11:00 UTC.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:25.732
Australia, two hours later.

00:00:25.732 --> 00:00:30.636
Japan at 15:00. India at 18:30.

00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:35.385
Europe at 23:00. The UK at midnight.

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:42.669
Then, at 05:00 UTC, the United States and Canada unlock together —

00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:45.704
midnight Eastern, 9 PM Pacific.

00:00:46.204 --> 00:00:49.732
Nineteen hours between the first player and the last.

00:00:50.232 --> 00:00:53.191
By the time a New Yorker starts the prologue,

00:00:53.191 --> 00:00:56.808
a player in Auckland has been inside Vice City for eighteen hours.

00:00:57.308 --> 00:01:01.635
Your exact unlock time is pinned in the comments.

00:01:01.635 --> 00:01:04.340
Look beyond what seems obvious.

